            "title": "Incorrect return value in Hexo.prototype._generate promise chain",
            "severity": "high",
            "file": "lib/hexo/index.js",
            "line": 308,
            "explanation": "In the _generate method, when processing the results of generator functions, the code returns 'data ? result.concat(data) : data'. This is incorrect because if data is falsy (like undefined or null), the original accumulator 'result' will be lost, potentially ending the Promise.reduce with an unexpected value. The line before the change properly returned 'data ? result.concat(data) : result', preserving the accumulated result.",
            "suggestion": "Change the return statement back to 'return data ? result.concat(data) : result;' to correctly accumulate generator outputs."
          }
